{% if testRuns.latest %}

<h2 id="the-run">The latest run</h2>

{% set run = testRuns.latest %}
{% set volatile = true %}
{% include "partials/run-summary.njk" %}

<p>
    That workflow link is the point of this page. Everything below is reduced
    from a machine-readable report the run wrote about itself, and the link goes
    to the run, so nothing here has to be taken on trust.
</p>

<h2 id="trend">Trend</h2>

{% if testRuns.history.length > 1 %}
{% runTrend testRuns.history %}

<p>
    Suite size is the series that moves, because it grows as the site does. Both
    plots are scaled to the range they cover rather than to zero, and each says
    where its range starts. A run that recorded failures is ringed.
</p>

<p>
    The history is as deep as what has been committed, and no deeper. Records are
    produced by the runner and accepted by hand, so a gap is a commit nobody
    accepted a record for rather than a run that did not happen.
</p>
{% else %}
<p>
    Not yet. A trend needs more than one accepted record, and there is one. The
    plots appear here once a second run has been recorded; the section is
    deliberately empty rather than showing a single point as though it were a
    line.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="by-suite">By suite</h2>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Spec</th>
            <th scope="col">What it asserts</th>
            <th scope="col">Tests</th>
            <th scope="col">Passed</th>
            <th scope="col">Failed</th>
            <th scope="col">Skipped</th>
            <th scope="col">Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {% for suite in testRuns.latest.suites %}
        <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>{{ suite.file }}</code></th>
            <td>
                {{ suite.purpose }}
                {% if suite.projects.length > 1 %}<span class="run-projects">Runs twice: {{ suite.projects | join(" and ") }}.</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ suite.tests }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ suite.passed }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ suite.failed }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ suite.skipped }}</td>
            <td class="numeric" data-volatile>{{ (suite.ms / 1000) | round }}s</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    The times are the sum of every test in that file, not wall clock. The suite
    runs in parallel across workers, so they add up to more than the run took.
</p>

{% if testRuns.latest.failures.length %}
<h2 id="failures">Failures</h2>

<p>
